  "solution": {
    "text": "We have, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced></mfrac></math><br />When <math><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1,2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, then <math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>⇒</mo><msub><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>4,10</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br />When <math><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2,3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, then <math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>⇒</mo><msub><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>5,10</mn></mrow></mfenced></math><br />When <math><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>3,4</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, then <math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>⇒</mo><msub><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>20</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>34</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math><br /><math><mo>∴</mo><msub><mrow><mi>R</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>34</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></math><br />Clearly, for <math><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1,2</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mfenced open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2,3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> range of <math><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> has common elements<br /><math><mo>⇒</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is many-one<br /><math><mo>⇒</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfenced></math> is not bijective"
